# Zurgo's mobilize 2 (CR 702.181a) makes two tapped and attacking 1/1 Warriors on turn 3, and mobilize sacrifices them at the
# beginning of the next end step. That end step is Bot1's own, and during it Zurgo gives Warrior tokens Bot1 controls "can't be
# sacrificed" (CR 604.1, 613.1f, 701.21a), so the delayed sacrifice does nothing and both are still on the battlefield, having
# dealt 4 to Bot2 with Zurgo (2+1+1). Checked in the end step itself, as the expectation block runs after the turn is over.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Zurgo, Thunder's Decree
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Zurgo, Thunder's Decree.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Zurgo, Thunder's Decree > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Warrior Token#2.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Warrior Token#1.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield.Warrior Token#2.Colors = Red
Bot1.Battlefield.Warrior Token#1.Colors = Red
